00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:48.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:50.000
teresa: But I haven't been doing it that way.

00:22:49.000 --> 00:23:06.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. Yeah, no. And you don't have to do it that way. If you would prefer for there to be a conversation, you decide upon a tour time, and then you book the tour for them. You totally can. So I assume that you're like going into your app and like scheduling a tour from the app, so that they're then receiving the confirmation and.

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:07.000
teresa: Yes.

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Reminder emails and texts, right?

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:11.000
teresa: Correct. Mm-hmm. That's fine.

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, perfect. So you can totally go about it, uh, the same way here. You know, we have the tour appointment, um, reminder workflows that are gonna, you know, confirm the tour.

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:23.000
Whitney Hodges: Um…

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:27.000
Whitney Hodges: Via text and via…

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Email, and then what we typically do is, um…

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:37.000
Whitney Hodges: Let's see, what they're doing, I guess, is…

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:40.000
Whitney Hodges: The day after the tour is scheduled.

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:55.000
Whitney Hodges: They're specifically asking if they have any questions. Is there anything that, you know, I can help you with before? They're including a link to a blog post to kind of create some, you know, anticipation there. And then a day before, they're sending a reminder email.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Um…

00:23:57.000 --> 00:24:12.000
Whitney Hodges: and a reminder text, and then an hour before a reminder email and a reminder text. But we can set up the cadence really to be. However, you'd like what we do like to do, though, with these pre tour emails is to.

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:14.000
Whitney Hodges: You know, really make sure that.

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:30.000
Whitney Hodges: they're not just confirmations or reminders, right? They're an opportunity to be able to pre-sell people on the venue. So whatever information you feel like is powerful to include there that you want people to know before they come in. That's what we want to incorporate.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Essentially. Um…

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:41.000
Whitney Hodges: And then after people have a tour with you, are you putting them into a workflow, or are you putting them into different workflows, depending upon.

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:48.000
Whitney Hodges: how interested they are, or do you send out… fill out, like, a post-tour survey or something in Nurture Pro?

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:42.000
teresa: Yep.

00:24:46.000 --> 00:25:00.000
teresa: There is a post-tour follow-up, um, well, and I have the option to choose, like, after the tour, uh, like, there's a survey that comes to me, and I choose if they booked or not at the tour.

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:51.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:55.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:24:56.000 --> 00:24:58.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:24:58.000 --> 00:25:01.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:04.000
teresa: And if they did not vote, then they get, um…

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:19.000
teresa: like, a follow-up email, and then I'll try to get… I usually will go in and offer them to… if they would like to come back, just the two of them, and do a walkthrough on their own. Just… I give them a door code, let them come in. I find that that… it's helped.

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:08.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:14.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Nice.

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:19.000
Whitney Hodges: Oh, cool!

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:29.000
teresa: like, I've booked a couple of people this summer after they did that. It's like, you know, there's a lot of noise when they bring family members.

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:27.000
Whitney Hodges: Wow. Oh, that's a cool idea.

00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:39.000
teresa: or somebody, and they're like, they brought their sister, but the sister's getting on their nerves. You know, just things like that. Anyway, so I like to… but I usually do that.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:35.000
Whitney Hodges: Good.

00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:37.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Yep.

