00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:06.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, makes sense.

00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:07.000
teresa: It's good to get that word out.

00:31:06.000 --> 00:31:24.000
Whitney Hodges: Yes, yeah, yeah, exactly. Those open house events are fun, especially to have like vendors come in and feature their stuff. And you know the the space is a little bit more dressed up usually than it would be, you know, just for for a tour. The other thing that we are starting to have our clients use.

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:13.000
teresa: Mm-hmm.

00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:39.000
Whitney Hodges: lead block for and what we've actually started to do ourselves is market research surveys. So sending, and I have a training on this in the vault as well, if you ever want to check it out. But it's meant to be sent out.

00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:56.000
Whitney Hodges: to your clients really very shortly after they book with you, right? When the buying decision is still very top of mind for them. So it's different than like a feedback survey that would go out after their wedding, right? Six months, a year later sort of thing, asking about how the event went.

00:31:56.000 --> 00:32:14.000
Whitney Hodges: The purpose of the survey is to really ask them why they booked with you, what the deciding factors were, what other venues maybe they toured, what were the most important deciding factors sort of thing. So that's something that very easily can be built in LeadBlock as well.

00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:28.000
Whitney Hodges: you know, have a link that goes to that survey, and, um, you know, you could even send the email out from HoneyBook if you wanted to, just so long as they get the LeadLock link, but then you can really start, um.

00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:43.000
Whitney Hodges: you know, strategically collecting data about who your your couples actually are. Obviously, you're gonna know a lot about your couples from just doing tours with them and kind of like getting to know them. But it can be really powerful when you're hearing from them in their own words about.

00:32:37.000 --> 00:32:39.000
teresa: Yep.

00:32:43.000 --> 00:33:03.000
Whitney Hodges: why they decided, you know, to to book with you right, or what kind of factors really kind of pushed them over the edge, because when you have that information, then that can be woven back into, you know your ad copy, or what you're including on your website or your landing pages to really be able to like be attracting those people in from the beginning.

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:08.000
teresa: Yeah, okay. Yeah, that sounds good.

00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:07.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, yeah.

00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:15.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. So there's a ton that you can do with it. I mean, the the possibilities are are limitless, really, but but that's, kind of what we're seeing on our end.

