00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:46.000
teresa: Mm-hmm. Yeah, I agree. And they… they can probably step in and help with some of that, too. So, it would be good if it's easy for them to just be able to go in and do it.

00:34:40.000 --> 00:34:42.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm, yeah.

00:34:45.000 --> 00:35:03.000
Whitney Hodges: Right, right. So, um, I'll, I'll show you this, and I can, uh, email this over to you as well. This essentially just kind of breaks down, um, you know, what the, uh, the scope is, and what the, the process is, really, for us to.

00:34:53.000 --> 00:34:55.000
teresa: Okay.

00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:16.000
Whitney Hodges: uh, to get you going inside of, of LeadLock. Um, we call this offer our foolproof follow-up advantage. So, um, really what the, the process looks like is, um.

00:35:16.000 --> 00:35:33.000
Whitney Hodges: First and foremost, we would have you fill out a pretty in-depth onboarding questionnaire for us to help us understand the venue and, you know, who your ideal client is, because we want to keep that in mind as we are, you know, customizing all of these emails and text messages for you.

00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:41.000
Whitney Hodges: Uh, there will be questions in there about your branding, um, as well, because, you know, if we're gonna create any sort of, um…

00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:56.000
Whitney Hodges: you know, forms that go on your website, we want, which we will, we'll want those to be on brand. If you ever want to go down the road of actually having a tour booking landing page that we create for you, we would want that to be on brand, um, as well.

00:35:56.000 --> 00:36:09.000
Whitney Hodges: But you'll have a, uh, a one-hour kickoff call with Danielle. She heads up all of our lead block setups, um, and you'll just kind of go over with her, um, kind of, uh.

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:05.000
teresa: Okay.

00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:24.000
Whitney Hodges: you know, a refresher of like what we went over today of like exactly how you would like to to utilize the the system right? And we'll do some initial connections on that call as far as you know, connecting your email account. You know your calendar.

00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:39.000
Whitney Hodges: uh, things like that, right, to kind of, like, make it all work. And then, um, of course, we can, you know, connect with Elizabeth on getting those DNS records, um, created, all of that. Um, and then from there, that's really when our team gets to work on.

00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:56.000
Whitney Hodges: building out the workflows, customizing all of the emails and text messages, everything like that. And, um, it's usually about, like, a 3-week process for us to do that, since it is very custom, but once we have those ready for you.

00:36:56.000 --> 00:37:11.000
Whitney Hodges: everything will get sent over to you for your review. We'll actually have you kind of, you know, experience it like a potential client would. You'll opt in for the form, and then you'll start receiving the emails and text messages. We'll push all of those emails and text messages out to you so you can review them.

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:27.000
Whitney Hodges: and then you can let us know of any changes that you'd like to see. And then, once those changes are in place, that's when we get on another call. This is really your official onboarding, because it is where we.

00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:43.000
